From: j7 g3d
Subject: j7prime: Mali-T830 job manager core + j7gpu=6 kernel selftest

j7gpu=5 passed on the phone (job irq 0x2, MMU/GPU clean, output zeroed). This is the next layer,
the part a user-space driver will sit on, exercised from the kernel first so it can be verified
from the boot log alone:

- page tables: four-level Mali-LPAE carved from a 2 MiB physically contiguous pool, same
  descriptor formats the A5 test proved (table|3, leaf pa|0x2c1, TRANSTAB root|7, memattr 0x888d88)
- BOs: IOBufferMemoryDescriptor pages (scattered is fine) mapped 4 KiB at a time at first-fit GPU
  VAs below 2 GiB (MMU_FEATURES 0x2821 = 33 VA bits), one guard page after each BO
- MMU: AS0 UPDATE, LOCK + FLUSH_PT over the exact range after map/unmap (Panfrost's sequence)
- jobs: JS_HEAD/AFFINITY/CONFIG/COMMAND_NEXT on a chosen slot, completion from JOB_IRQ_RAWSTAT,
  MMU faults reported, GPU soft reset recovery
- selftest (j7gpu=6): two chained WRITE_VALUE jobs writing across two BOs, free + re-create the
  BO at the same VA on different pages and run again (needs a correct flush), then a deliberate
  write to an unmapped VA that must fault cleanly, reset, free everything

Tested on the host against a simulated Mali with scattered physical pages, incoherent caches and
a stale-TLB model (the same code passes; with FLUSH_PT disabled the second chain is caught).
Not yet run on hardware.

